 199	
 200	## 7. Logit-Constrained Tool Calling & GBNF Engine (WP-1107)
 201	
 202	To prevent JSON argument parse failures and conversational rambling from open-weights models, Nexus v1.1.0 provides a logit-level constrained decoding engine targeting near-zero repair retries on supported inference backends:
 203	
 204	```
 205	Registered Tools ──► Tool Schema Compiler ──► GBNF / Outlines Grammar ──► Local Engine (llama.cpp / vLLM)
 206	                                                                                   │
 207	Model Sampling Logits: Token Masking (-∞ for schema-invalid tokens) ◄──────────────┘
 208	                                    │
 209	                                    ▼
 210	       Schema-Compliant Tool Call Payload (repair_rate target = 0.0)
 211	```
 212	
 213	### 7.1 Dynamic GBNF Grammar Generation
 214	Nexus compiles registered tool definitions (`run_command`, `read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`) into a strict Context-Free Grammar conforming to GGML GBNF:
 215	
 216	```ebnf
 217	root        ::= ws (thought ws)? tool-call ws
 218	thought     ::= "<think>" [^<]* "</think>"
 219	tool-call   ::= "{" ws "\"name\":" ws tool-name "," ws "\"args\":" ws tool-args "}"
 220	tool-name   ::= "\"run_command\"" | "\"read_file\"" | "\"write_file\"" | "\"edit_file\""
 221	tool-args   ::= run-args | read-args | write-args | edit-args
 222	
 223	run-args    ::= "{" ws "\"CommandLine\":" ws string "," ws "\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":" ws integer ("," ws "\"IsDaemon\":" ws boolean)? "}"
 224	read-args   ::= "{" ws "\"Path\":" ws string ("," ws "\"StartLine\":" ws integer)? ("," ws "\"EndLine\":" ws integer)? "}"
